Negative control for the gate offering the arrival a choice (`R7-1`).

Puts the guard's rejection back to naming an actor unconditionally. The url said
nothing about who is arriving, so `authCollectActor` supplies its CLIENT
fallback and the target carries `as=client` — which is indistinguishable, at the
overlay, from an entry that genuinely asked for a client session. The overlay
then reads an actor as NAMED, skips the chooser, and a guest or staff arrival is
locked into the client journey with no way to say otherwise. That is exactly the
defect: the fallback is a sensible answer to "which journey do we collect", and
a disastrous one to "who is arriving".

Nothing else moves — the add-session arm still names its own actor, the cancel
landing is untouched, and the overlay's own chooser code is left in place — so a
red here is the gate's arrival choice and not a crash. Watch for the pool cases:
they must stay GREEN, since they were always the arm that names its own actor,
and that is what makes this a control and not a rewrite.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: auth-overlay.spec.ts — the case landing on a guarded page whose url names
no actor and expecting the client/staff/guest chooser with nothing collected
until it is answered. The pool/add-session cases (an entry that named its own
actor shows NO chooser and opens straight on that journey) stay green by
construction; if they go red too, the control has been over-applied.

  FOR THE PROVER: authored by the developer seat, which knew the line to mutate;
  it carries no verification run. Apply it blind, confirm the arrival-choice
  case goes red and the pool cases stay green, then revert.

--- a/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/app/funnels/labs.ts
+++ b/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/app/funnels/labs.ts
@@ -128,9 +128,7 @@
         [ADD_SESSION_PARAM]: Date.now().toString()
       }
     : {
-        ...(authNamedActor(named)
-          ? { [ACTOR_PARAM]: toString(named) }
-          : undefined),
+        [ACTOR_PARAM]: toString(authCollectActor(named)),
         [MODE_PARAM]: SESSION_FORMS.LOGIN,
         [QUERY_PARAMS.CANCEL_URL]: ROUTE.HOME
       };
